{TEXT 270 22 "MAPLE NOTES for MA321 " }}{PARA 260 "" 0 "" {TEXT 271 
55 "School of Mathematics, Statistics & Applied Mathematics" }{TEXT 
-1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 
144 "These notes are a review of basic features of Maple 13 and an int
roduction to some advanced aspects. Please proceed by entering return \+
at each >" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 14 "prompt symbol." }}}{EXCHG 
{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 258 "" 0 "" {TEXT 
256 27 "3. Functions and Calculus. " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }
}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 111 "Here we describe the use of functions, \+
differentiation and integration in Maple. This includes a discussion o
f:" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {HYPERLNK 17 "fu
nction definition arrow symbol" 1 "" "function" }{TEXT -1 3 " , " }}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {HYPERLNK 17 "@ function composition operator" 1 "" "a
t" }{TEXT -1 3 " , " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {HYPERLNK 17 "diff - Differenti
ation" 1 "" "diff" }{TEXT -1 3 " , " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {HYPERLNK 17 "i
nt - Integration" 1 "" "int" }{TEXT -1 2 " ," }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{HYPERLNK 17 "D operator" 1 "" "D" }{TEXT -1 3 " ,\n" }{HYPERLNK 17 "P
artial differentiation" 1 "" "partial" }{TEXT -1 2 " ," }}{PARA 0 "" 
0 "" {HYPERLNK 17 "dsolve" 1 "" "dsolve" }{TEXT -1 2 ".\n" }}{PARA 0 "
> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "function" {TEXT 257 18 "Functions in Maple" }{TEXT -1 
103 ". User-defined functions of one or more variables are defined by \+
use of the arrow symbol -> as follows:" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "
" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 40 "> functionname := variable -> express
ion" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 57 "> functionname := (variable1,varia
ble2,...) -> expression" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 
0 "" {TEXT -1 115 "These functions can then be manipulated and evaluat
ed like sytem-defined Maple functions such as ln(x), cos(x) etc." }}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 10 "Examples:
\n" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 10 "f:=y->y^2;" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "
" {XPPMATH 20 "6#>%\"fGf*6#%\"yG6\"6$%)operatorG%&arrowGF(*$)9$\"\"#\"
\"\"F(F(F(" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 8 "f(x);   " }}
{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#*$)%\"xG\"\"#\"\"\"" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 
0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 5 "f(5);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#
\"#D" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 22 "g:=(x,y)->x*y - 3*y
^2;" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#>%\"gGf*6$%\"xG%\"yG6\"6$%)oper
atorG%&arrowGF),&*&9$\"\"\"9%F0F0*&\"\"$F0)F1\"\"#F0!\"\"F)F)F)" }}}
{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 9 "print(g);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "
" {XPPMATH 20 "6#f*6$%\"xG%\"yG6\"6$%)operatorG%&arrowGF',&*&9$\"\"\"9
%F.F.*&\"\"$F.)F/\"\"#F.!\"\"F'F'F'" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 0 10 "g(10,2);\n\n" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#\"\")
" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "at" {TEXT 258 44 "@ - Composition of Functio
ns of One Variable" }{TEXT -1 32 ". We may form a new function of " }
{TEXT 259 3 "one" }{TEXT -1 55 " variable by the composition of two gi
ven functions of " }{TEXT 260 3 "one" }{TEXT -1 21 " variable as follo
ws:" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 37 "> \+
newfunction := function1@function2;" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }
}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 39 "Thus (f@g)(x) is the function f(g(x)). \+
" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 78 "@@ - Repeated Compositions. T
o repeatedly compose the same function n times : " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 29 "> newfunction := function
@@n;" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 27 "T
hus (f@@3)(x)=f(f(f(x))). " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 
"" 0 "" {TEXT -1 11 "Examples: \n" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 
19 "restart: f:=x->x^2;" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#>%\"fGf*6#%
\"xG6\"6$%)operatorG%&arrowGF(*$)9$\"\"#\"\"\"F(F(F(" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 
0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 14 "g:=y->1/(1-y);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" 
{XPPMATH 20 "6#>%\"gGf*6#%\"yG6\"6$%)operatorG%&arrowGF(*&\"\"\"F-,&F-
F-9$!\"\"F0F(F(F(" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 9 "(g@f)(x
);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#*&\"\"\"F$,&F$F$*$)%\"xG\"\"#F$!
\"\"F*" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 9 "(f@g)(y);" }}
{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#*&\"\"\"F$*$),&F$F$%\"yG!\"\"\"\"#F$F)
" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 10 "(f@@4)(u);" }}{PARA 11 
"" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#*$)%\"uG\"#;\"\"\"" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "diff" {TEXT 261 19 "Calculus with Maple
" }{TEXT -1 166 ".  Differentiation and integration are both featured \+
in Maple. Some types of differential equations can also be solved expl
icitly or approximately by various methods." }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 
-1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 262 22 "diff - Differentiation" }
{TEXT -1 96 ".  The ordinary derivative of a given expression with res
pect to a given variable x is given by " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 
"" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 22 "> diff(expression, x);" }}{PARA 0 "
" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 10 "Examples :" }}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 25 "res
tart: diff(x^2+2*x,x);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#,&*&\"\"#\"
\"\"%\"xGF&F&F%F&" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 23 "diff(A
*cos(omega*t),t);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#,$*(%\"AG\"\"\"-%
$sinG6#*&%&omegaGF&%\"tGF&F&F+F&!\"\"" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 83 "Multiple derivatives of a
n expression with respect to a given variable are given by" }}{PARA 0 
"" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 31 "> diff(expression
, x, x,...,x);" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT -1 10 "Example :\n" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 12 "f:=x->x
^4-x;" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#>%\"fGf*6#%\"xG6\"6$%)operato
rG%&arrowGF(,&*$)9$\"\"%\"\"\"F1F/!\"\"F(F(F(" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 
0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 28 "diff(f(x),x);diff(f(x),x,x);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "
" {XPPMATH 20 "6#,&*&\"\"%\"\"\")%\"xG\"\"$F&F&F&!\"\"" }}{PARA 11 "" 
1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#,$*&\"#7\"\"\")%\"xG\"\"#F&F&" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "
" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "D" {TEXT 263 42 "D - Operator Dif
ferentiation of a Function" }{TEXT -1 115 ".  There is a useful shorth
and notation for the ordinary derivatives of a function of a single va
riable as follows:" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT -1 32 "> derivative := D(functionname);" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT -1 41 "> secondderivative := D(D(functionname));" }}{PARA 0 "" 
0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 100 "defines the functio
ns which are the first and second order derivatives of functionname re
spectively." }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "
" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 85 "Multiple derivatives ca
n also be given by use of the @@ repeated composition symbol: " }}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 41 "> secondd
erivative:=(D@@2)(functionname);" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 10 "Examples:\n" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 0 9 "print(f);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#f*6#%\"xG
6\"6$%)operatorG%&arrowGF&,&*$)9$\"\"%\"\"\"F/F-!\"\"F&F&F&" }}}
{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 13 "D(f);D(f)(u);" }}{PARA 11 "
" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#f*6#%\"xG6\"6$%)operatorG%&arrowGF&,&*&\"\"%\"\"
\")9$\"\"$F-F-F-!\"\"F&F&F&" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#,&*&\"
\"%\"\"\")%\"uG\"\"$F&F&F&!\"\"" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 
1 0 10 "(D@@3)(f);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#f*6#%\"xG6\"6$%)
operatorG%&arrowGF&,$*&\"#C\"\"\"9$F-F-F&F&F&" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 
"" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "int" {TEXT 264 17 "int - Integration
" }{TEXT -1 71 ". The indefinite integral of any expression over a var
iable is found by" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT -1 27 "> int(expression,variable);" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 
0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 73 "The definite integral over a varia
ble range from low to high is given by " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 
"" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 38 "> int(expression, variable=low..high
);" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 10 "Exa
mples:\n" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 16 "int(cos(x/2),x);" }}
{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#,$*&\"\"#\"\"\"-%$sinG6#,$*&F%!\"\"%\"
xGF&F&F&F&" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT -1 46 "Note that no constant of integration is shown." }}{PARA 
0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 21 " f:=x->x^
2-3*exp(-x);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#>%\"fGf*6#%\"xG6\"6$%)
operatorG%&arrowGF(,&*$)9$\"\"#\"\"\"F1*&\"\"$F1-%$expG6#,$F/!\"\"F1F8
F(F(F(" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 20 " int(f(x),x = 0..
1);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#,&#\"\")\"\"$!\"\"*&F&\"\"\"-%$
expG6#F'F)F)" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 32 " int(exp(-x
^2),x = 0..infinity);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#,$*&\"\"#!\"
\"%#PiG#\"\"\"F%F)" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 29 "The famous \+
Gaussian integral." }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 
"" 0 "" {TEXT -1 124 "If the integral cannot be evaluated exactly then
 an approximate numerical solution can be found by use of the evalf co
mmand:" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 9 "
Example:\n" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 38 "int(exp(-x^4)/(1+exp(
sin(x))),x=0..1);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#-%$intG6$*&-%$exp
G6#,$*$)%\"xG\"\"%\"\"\"!\"\"F/,&F/F/-F(6#-%$sinG6#F-F/F0/F-;\"\"!F/" 
}}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 
1 0 9 "evalf(%);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#$\"+^$HzP$!#5" }}}
{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 265 3 "In
t" }{TEXT -1 70 " - the unevaluated Integral can be directly reproduce
d by the command " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT -1 27 "> Int(expression,variable);" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 
45 "> Int(expression,variable,variable=low,high);" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 9 "Example:\n" }}{PARA 0 "> \+
" 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 56 "Int(x^2*cos(4*x),x=-Pi..Pi)=int(x^2*cos(4*x),x
=-Pi..Pi);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#/-%$IntG6$*&)%\"xG\"\"#
\"\"\"-%$cosG6#,$*&\"\"%F+F)F+F+F+/F);,$%#PiG!\"\"F5,$*&F1F6F5F+F+" }}
}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "partial" {TEXT 
266 23 "Partial Differentiation" }{TEXT -1 86 ".  Partial differentiat
ion of an expression can also be performed by the diff command:" }}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 45 "> diff(ex
pression, variable1, variable2,...);" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" 
}}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 9 "Example:\n" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 0 26 "g:=(x,y)-> x*y^3 - 3*x*y ;" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" 
{XPPMATH 20 "6#>%\"gGf*6$%\"xG%\"yG6\"6$%)operatorG%&arrowGF),&*&9$\"
\"\")9%\"\"$F0F0*(F3F0F/F0F2F0!\"\"F)F)F)" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "
" {MPLTEXT 1 0 17 "diff(g(x,y),x,y);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "
6#,&*&\"\"$\"\"\")%\"yG\"\"#F&F&F%!\"\"" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 267 44 "D[i] - Partial Different
iation of a Function" }{TEXT -1 219 ". The D operator can also be used
 to obtain partial derivatives of a function of many variables where D
[1] denotes partial differentiation with respect to the first variable
 etc. Thus repeating the last example we find:" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 9 "print(g);" }}{PARA 
11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#f*6$%\"xG%\"yG6\"6$%)operatorG%&arrowGF',&*&
9$\"\"\")9%\"\"$F.F.*(F1F.F-F.F0F.!\"\"F'F'F'" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 
0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 14 "D[1](D[2](g));" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "
6#f*6$%\"xG%\"yG6\"6$%)operatorG%&arrowGF',&*&\"\"$\"\"\")9%\"\"#F.F.F
-!\"\"F'F'F'" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "
" {TEXT -1 92 "gives the function formed by taking the y derivative fo
llowed by the x derivative of g(x,y)." }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "dsolve" {TEXT 268 39 "dsolve - Solving D
ifferential Equations" }{TEXT -1 191 ".  Maple has a range of packages
 and methods for solving some differential equations explicitly. Appro
ximate solutions can also be found such as power series solutions or n
umerical solutions." }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "
" {TEXT -1 105 "The simplest example is to solve a given differential \+
equation for a function depending on some variable." }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "
" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 39 "> dsolve(equation, func
tion(variable));" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT -1 9 "Examples:" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "> " 
0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 50 "restart:with(DEtools):deq1:=diff(y(x),x)-4*y(x)=
2;" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#>%%deq1G/,&-%%diffG6$-%\"yG6#%\"
xGF-\"\"\"*&\"\"%F.F*F.!\"\"\"\"#" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 0 18 "dsolve(deq1,y(x));" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6
#/-%\"yG6#%\"xG,&#\"\"\"\"\"#!\"\"*&-%$expG6#,$*&\"\"%F*F'F*F*F*%$_C1G
F*F*" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 50 "Note the appearance of an
 arbitrary constant _C1 !" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "
> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 38 "deq2 := (D@@2)(x)(t)+omega^2*x(t) = 0;" }}
{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#>%%deq2G/,&---%#@@G6$%\"DG\"\"#6#%\"xG
6#%\"tG\"\"\"*&)%&omegaGF-F2-F/F0F2F2\"\"!" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "
" {MPLTEXT 1 0 18 "dsolve(deq2,x(t));" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 
"6#/-%\"xG6#%\"tG,&*&%$_C1G\"\"\"-%$sinG6#*&%&omegaGF+F'F+F+F+*&%$_C2G
F+-%$cosGF.F+F+" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 
0 "" {TEXT 269 18 "Initial Conditions" }{TEXT -1 96 ". Initial conditi
ons on the unknown function and its derivatives can also be supplied i
n dsolve:" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 
73 "> dsolve(set of an equation and initial condition(s),function(vari
able));" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 
32 "Sets will be discussed later on." }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" 
}}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 9 "Example:\n" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 0 42 "dsolve(\{deq2,x(0)=x0, (D(x))(0)=v0\},x(t));" }}
{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#/-%\"xG6#%\"tG,&*(%#v0G\"\"\"%&omegaG!
\"\"-%$sinG6#*&F,F+F'F+F+F+*&%#x0GF+-%$cosGF0F+F+" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 18 
"" 0 "" {TEXT -1 42 "The numerical solution of ODEs using Maple" }}
{PARA 19 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 437 
"Most ordinary differential equations cannot be solve analytically. If
 Maple cannot find the solution in terms of functions it knows about, \+
it won't suceed in finding a solution. In such circumstances, we can m
ake use of Maple's numeric solvers. You are advised to carefully read \+
the 'numeric' helpfile for 'dsolve'. We illustrate with a simple examp
le; suppose we wish to numerically integrate the following simple init
ial value problem:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6$/-%%Diff
G6$-%\"yG6#%\"tGF*,$F'!\"\"/-F(6#\"\"!\"\"\"" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "
